LAB PATCH for freifunkMUC/uradvd main-parker-new
(9c44a2cae9e3573047f152c716950807767a8da3). Not upstream yet.

One uradvd instance announces all prefixes of a node in one RA, each with
its own lifetimes:
  -a/-p <prefix>[,<preferred>[,<valid>]]
  --state-file <file>   lines "<prefix>[,<preferred>[,<valid>]]" or
                        "rdnss <ip>". Read at start and on SIGHUP; after
                        SIGHUP three RAs go out, 3 s apart, the first at once.
                        A bad file is ignored.

Why: two instances on one link send from the same link-local address, and
each RA leaves out the prefix of the other one. dhcpcd (and other clients
that track the prefixes of a router) then deprecate the missing prefix.

Apply with: patch -p1 < uradvd.patch
Test with:  multipop/tests/uradvd-smoke.sh (needs docker)

